::ENG4_U04_L07_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.W.03] Passage: A paper coastline map and a digital risk model are shown together. Which claim is most analytical?
{
~A. The room has maps and a screen.#Incorrect. This summarizes setting without interpreting meaning.
=B. The contrast between paper and digital maps shows that future planning depends on understanding the past.#Correct. This interprets the function of the contrast.
~C. Elena is standing in a room.#Incorrect. This is a literal detail, not analysis.
~D. The passage includes blue lines.#Incorrect. This identifies a detail without explaining function.
}

::ENG4_U04_L07_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG4.W.02] Which evidence best supports the claim that the passage contrasts memory and prediction?
{
~A. "The map room was the quietest place in the building."#Incorrect. This establishes setting but less directly supports the contrast.
~B. "Elena traced one curve with her finger."#Incorrect. This is useful detail but not the strongest evidence for the claim.
~C. "The new digital model glowed."#Incorrect. This supports only one side of the contrast.
=D. "The future... was not a clean replacement for the past. It was an argument with it."#Correct. This line directly supports the interpretation.
}

::ENG4_U04_L07_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG4.W.04] Which revision improves "The maps are different"?
{
=A. The paper map and digital model create a contrast between remembered storms and projected risk.#Correct. This revision adds precise analytical meaning.
~B. The maps are very different and different.#Incorrect. This repeats the same idea.
~C. The maps are in the room and one is paper.#Incorrect. This adds detail but not analysis.
~D. The maps are about things.#Incorrect. This is vague.
}

::ENG4_U04_L07_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Which sentence uses "function" accurately?
{
~A. The function is that I liked the passage.#Incorrect. Function means the job a choice performs, not personal preference.
~B. Function means the passage has a title.#Incorrect. A title is not the definition of function.
=C. The function of the contrast is to show that prediction and memory both shape planning.#Correct. This accurately explains what the contrast does.
~D. The function is to use random words.#Incorrect. This is not accurate academic use.
}

::ENG4_U04_L07_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG4.W.03] Passage: "The stage details function as remnants of collaboration." What makes this analysis strong?
{
~A. It lists every object in the passage.#Incorrect. Listing alone is not analysis.
=B. It explains what the details do and connects them to a larger meaning.#Correct. Strong analysis explains function and meaning.
~C. It avoids evidence completely.#Incorrect. Analysis needs evidence.
~D. It summarizes the plot only.#Incorrect. Summary alone is not analysis.
}
